# Mobi Knowledge Base — usage rules

The **Mobi Knowledge Base** MCP server is available. Use it whenever you need
information from the organisation's knowledge base, BC/AL documentation, uploaded
documents, or connector specifications.

## BC vs Mobi routing

| Context                                                               | Tool                                  |
| --------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------- |
| Business Central, AL, tag-bc, codeunits, tables, pages, `.al` files   | `search_bc_knowledge`                 |
| Mobi platform, frontend, API, connectors, configuration, "how do I …" | `search_knowledge`                    |
| Issue spans both                                                      | call both tools with tailored queries |

## Tool selection guide

| Situation                                        | Tool                                                                |
| ------------------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| General "how does X work" (Mobi)                 | `search_knowledge`                                                  |
| "How do I create / configure / use …" (Mobi)     | `search_knowledge` — use `layer` when known                         |
| BC domain, AL objects, posting flows             | `search_bc_knowledge`                                               |
| Content from an uploaded file (PDF, Word, Excel) | `search_documents`                                                  |
| Connector-specific lookup                        | `search_collection` with `connector_knowledge` or `connector_specs` |
| Exploring what's available                       | `list_collections`                                                  |

## Do not use `search_business_answers`

`search_business_answers` is **broken** on the hosted server (Qdrant requires a
named vector: `answer` or `question`). Calling it returns an error. For FAQ-style
or procedural questions, use `search_knowledge` instead.

## Layer and category hints (Mobi)

Pass `layer` on `search_knowledge` when the domain is clear:

- `layer1-configuration` — setup, config, admin
- `layer2-frontend-flows` — UI flows, user-facing guides
- `business_logic` — domain rules and behaviour

Pass `category` to narrow scope: `overview`, `integration`, `api`, `guide`, etc.

## Always filter by tenant when known

If you know the `tenant_id`, always pass it:

```json
{ "query": "...", "tenant_id": "the-tenant-id" }
```

## Score threshold

Default is `0.3`. For high-precision answers, raise to `0.6–0.75`. For broad
discovery, leave at `0.3` or lower.

## Analyzing a work item

When analyzing an issue, ticket, or task end-to-end (knowledge + code), follow
the `analyze-work-item` skill.

## Result shape

Each result includes: `title`, `file_name`, `file_path`, `layer`, `category`,
`tags`, `score`, and content fields. Always cite `title` and `file_path` (or
`heading` when present) when surfacing knowledge to the user.
